# Start the Lua worker only while the timer is on - it does nothing otherwise,
# and on most nodes the timer is off. On 64 MB devices (Archer C25) the file
# cache is too small to keep Lua between two minutes: every start came from
# flash, 450-900 ms a minute; the uci check costs about 100 ms.
# (micrond cuts each line at the first hash sign - the command must not use one.)
# "on" in any spelling OpenWrt accepts for a boolean (1/true/yes/on/enabled).
* * * * * case "$(uci -q get ap-timer.settings.enabled)" in 1|true|yes|on|enabled) /usr/sbin/ap-timer ;; esac
